From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:00:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] RendererDRMPRIMEGLES: Take over formats the video plane
 rejects

With direct to plane selected, a DRM PRIME buffer no plane can scan out
(the MediaTek planes take neither YUV420 nor S010 from the software
decoder) ended up at the default GLES renderer, which cannot render
drm_prime at all. Since the plane renderer is tried first, accepting
these buffers here only adds a fallback.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../VideoRenderers/HwDecRender/RendererDRMPRIMEGLES.cpp      | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/HwDecRender/RendererDRMPRIMEGLES.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/HwDecRender/RendererDRMPRIMEGLES.cpp
index 5bea716ad9..413dd14cb9 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/HwDecRender/RendererDRMPRIMEGLES.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/HwDecRender/RendererDRMPRIMEGLES.cpp
@@ -45,9 +45,8 @@ CBaseRenderer* CRendererDRMPRIMEGLES::Create(CVideoBuffer* buffer)
   if (!settings->GetBool(CSettings::SETTING_VIDEOPLAYER_USEPRIMEDECODER))
     return nullptr;
 
-  if (settings->GetInt(CSettings::SETTING_VIDEOPLAYER_USEPRIMERENDERER) != 1)
-    return nullptr;
-
+  // with direct to plane selected, "drm_prime" is tried first, so this only
+  // takes over the formats no video plane can scan out
   auto buf = dynamic_cast<CVideoBufferDRMPRIME*>(buffer);
   if (!buf)
     return nullptr;
